Fix folder-source drag disable, bookmark reorder direction, and horizontal resize line

- Folder entries remain valid drop targets but are no longer draggable sources. This is explicitly marked DISABLED ONLY; the previous draggable assignments and underlying drag handler remain in the code. Leaf bookmarks inside folders and nested subfolders remain draggable.
- Permit native drag initiation from bookmark leaf rows in folder popovers and nested submenus.
- Correct same-parent bookmark reordering: preserve the target insertion index when calling Chrome's bookmarks.move rather than decrementing it twice. This fixes drops intended to move an earlier item below a later one.
- Disable the horizontal docked strip's bottom/top resize-line gesture, including its separate outside hit buffer. Vertical-mode resizing remains unchanged. The original grip markup/handler remains and is marked as disabled only.
- Existing overlay-drag behavior closes open menus at the movement threshold. Tab tooltips stay outside the horizontal/vertical tab strip.

Validation: edited JavaScript files pass syntax parsing and same-parent reorder cases were checked against the insertion-index calculation. No live Chrome UI test was run.
